  },
  data: {
    LLM: '1. Banker: One player is chosen by dice as banker; sets betting limits and deals.\n2. Deal: Banker deals five tiles to each player; players place bets.\n3. Discard: Each player chooses three tiles that total a multiple of 10 and discards them; the 4-2 and 2-1 tiles are wild (count as 3 or 6). If a player cannot form a multiple-of-10 discard, they lose their bet; if the banker cannot, the banker pays all who did and others get bets back.\n4. Score: Sum the pips on the two remaining tiles and take the last digit (mod 10). Higher than banker wins; lower loses; tie pushes.\n5. Bank: If the banker made a discard, the bank passes right; otherwise the banker keeps the bank.',
    Player: '1. Banker: One player is chosen by dice as banker; sets betting limits and deals.\n2. Deal: Banker deals five tiles to each player; players place bets.\n3. Discard: Each player chooses three tiles that total a multiple of 10 and discards them; the 4-2 and 2-1 tiles are wild (count as 3 or 6). If a player cannot form a multiple-of-10 discard, they lose their bet; if the banker cannot, the banker pays all who did and others get bets back.\n4. Score: Sum the pips on the two remaining tiles and take the last digit (mod 10). Higher than banker wins; lower loses; tie pushes.\n5. Bank: If the banker made a discard, the bank passes right; otherwise the banker keeps the bank.',
    objective: "Have a higher hand than the banker: after discarding three tiles that total a multiple of 10, the sum of the two remaining tiles (modulo 10) must beat the banker's total.",
    gameplay: '1. Banker: One player is chosen by dice as banker; sets betting limits and deals.\n2. Deal: Banker deals five tiles to each player; players place bets.\n3. Discard: Each player chooses three tiles that total a multiple of 10 and discards them; the 4-2 and 2-1 tiles are wild (count as 3 or 6). If a player cannot form a multiple-of-10 discard, they lose their bet; if the banker cannot, the banker pays all who did and others get bets back.\n4. Score: Sum the pips on the two remaining tiles and take the last digit (mod 10). Higher than banker wins; lower loses; tie pushes.\n5. Bank: If the banker made a discard, the bank passes right; otherwise the banker keeps the bank.',
    keyRules: [
      'Discard exactly three tiles whose pips sum to a multiple of 10; wilds 4-2 and 2-1 may stand for 3 or 6.',
